{
  "id": "celery_celery_10837",
  "repo_name": "celery/celery",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/celery/celery",
  "base_commit": "2fa4aa287865e0d7c79a783d82050a3f6744f589",
  "pr_number": 10837,
  "issue_number": 7894,
  "issue_title": "Celery not configuring flower subcommand for user-defined preload CLI options",
  "issue_body": "Per the [documentation][1], users may add a command-line option that is passed to all sub-commands by adding a Click Option instance to `user_options['preload']`. \r\n\r\nWith this option, I've been able to pass an `--ini` cli option to the celery cli and configure my celery app from an ini file containing my application config.\r\n\r\nHowever, because this new option is also passed to all sub-commands, `flower` fails to start as it does not recognize the new argument. Since new user-added options appear to work for other sub-commands like worker, beat, and events, I'm wondering if this is a bug in that celery is not passing this new command option down to flower?\r\n\r\nThis works for the `worker`, `beat` and `events` subcommands:\r\n\r\n    $ celery -A example worker --ini app.ini\r\n    app.ini\r\n\r\nBut it fails for the `flower` subcommand:\r\n\r\n    $ celery -A example flower --ini app.ini\r\n\r\nThe traceback:\r\n\r\n    Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n      File \"/usr/local/bin/celery\", line 8, in <module>\r\n        sys.exit(main())\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/celery/__main__.py\", line 15, in main\r\n        sys.exit(_main())\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/celery/bin/celery.py\", line 217, in main\r\n        return celery(auto_envvar_prefix=\"CELERY\")\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/click/core.py\", line 1130, in __call__\r\n        return self.main(*args, **kwargs)\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/click/core.py\", line 1055, in main\r\n        rv = self.invoke(ctx)\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/click/core.py\", line 1657, in invoke\r\n        return _process_result(sub_ctx.command.invoke(sub_ctx))\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/click/core.py\", line 1404, in invoke\r\n        return ctx.invoke(self.callback, **ctx.params)\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/click/core.py\", line 760, in invoke\r\n        return __callback(*args, **kwargs)\r\n      File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.8/dist-packages/click/decorators.py\", line 26, in new_func\r\n        return f(get_current_context(), *args, **kwargs)\r\n    TypeError: flower() got an unexpected keyword argument 'ini'\r\n\r\n\r\n**dependencies:**\r\n* celery==5.2.7\r\n* flower==1.2.0\r\n\r\n\r\n**example.py**\r\n\r\n    from celery import Celery\r\n    from celery import signals\r\n    from click import Option\r\n    \r\n    app = Celery()\r\n    \r\n    ini_option = Option(('-i', '--ini'), help='ini file path to use.')\r\n    \r\n    app.user_options['preload'].add(ini_option)\r\n    \r\n    @signals.user_preload_options.connect\r\n    def on_preload_parsed(options, **kwargs):\r\n        print(options['ini'])\r\n        exit(-1)\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://docs.celeryq.dev/en/latest/userguide/extending.html#preload-options\r\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-10-17T11:14:54Z",
